From 0369d95b15016061f925f8123eca7ed589e00695 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaloyan Naumov <knaumov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0014b-b70-offload-junction: heal a hybrid prefix after one
 miss (B70_OFFLOAD_JUNCTION=1)

Default off. On a hybrid (full attention + Mamba/GDN) model with sparse Mamba
retention (prefix_cache_retention_interval=0, the default), a request stores one
Mamba checkpoint at aligned(num_prompt_tokens-1). A revisit whose suffix differs
before that boundary finds full-attention chunks but no Mamba state at or below
the full-attention hit, so the whole lookup returns 0. The offload path never
sets a shared-prefix junction (only a GPU prefix-cache hit does,
kv_cache_manager.get_computed_blocks), so the recompute stores its checkpoint
inside the varying suffix again and the prefix misses forever.

With B70_OFFLOAD_JUNCTION=1, when the first Mamba group cuts the hit below
the boundary the full-attention groups confirmed, the connector sets
request.shared_prefix_boundary to that boundary (never lowering an existing
one). The core scheduler already honours it: the chunk splitter stops there,
MambaManager.cache_blocks adds it to reachable_boundaries so the state block is
hashed, and the aligned boundary hand-off stores it to the CPU tier. The first
revisit misses; later revisits hit.

Tests: tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/offloading_connector/test_b70_offload.py

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
