From bd64e11aef2b9b5b01ab8b9a6b40add07c35865d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaloyan Naumov <knaumov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 06:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0014f-b70-offload-gates: #51787 backport opt-in
 (B70_OFFLOAD_GROUP_EVICT=1); cheap TRACE=1

A mixed-load regression split showed that the 0014 build differed from the
serving build in eviction policy (0014e, ungated) and logged every lookup.
Make both opt-in.

GROUP_EVICT (default off = upstream v0.30.0, verbatim):
- cpu/policies/lru.py and arc.py restored to upstream; the vllm#51787 classes
  move to lru_group_evict.py / arc_group_evict.py (GroupEvict*CachePolicy) and
  are selected by CPUOffloadingManager only with the flag on (built-in names,
  no out-of-tree module path).
- flag off: prepare_store = upstream body (_prepare_store_upstream),
  prepare_load records no request access, on_request_finished/on_new_request
  do nothing for recency, and the scheduler's per-lookup / per-store _touch is
  back. Key-position bookkeeping in ReqContext stays (write-only when off).
- tests: the three upstream suites 0014e rewrote are restored; 0014e's
  versions live on as *_group_evict.py with GROUP_EVICT=1 set module-wide.

TRACE levels (B70_OFFLOAD_TRACE):
- 1: boot line, 60 s state line, and the mechanism events only
  (junction-set, zeroed_by a Mamba group), once per request per value.
- 2: plus every per-request lookup/store/load/handoff/req-done/guard line
  (the old 1). At TRACE=1 with vLLM at DEBUG they are emitted at DEBUG.
- at TRACE<2 the per-key LookupResult Counter is no longer built.
GUARD: skip the pending-key lookups when every offered key was stored.

CPU tests: flags off -> upstream suites fail set identical to the unpatched
baseline (34, GPU/weights-bound), group_evict suites 0 failures;
TRACE/JUNCTION/GUARD/BACKSTEP=1 -> +3 per scheduler suite, the known
guard-lookup tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
